//! **ByteV1 S1a: the Nat-keyed store and the function fetch** (crystal link 4, D20;
//! `designs/2026-10-01-evalir-bytev1-memory.md` §2.2 and §7).
//!
//! The ladder trie with full-key buckets that ByteV1's memory is built on, its laws, and the
//! function-table instance W4b needs: `ir_func_trie_find` says a fetch through the trie IS
//! `ir_func_find`. Every law is a STATE equation, proved by induction on the ladder or the list,
//! with no arithmetic about keys and no new accelerated constant (only `ir_nat_ltb`,
//! `ir_nat_eqb` and native `Nat.sub`).
//!
//! GENERATED by `reports/crystal-lane/2026-10-01-bytev1/s1a/emit_stage.py` from `gen_s1a.py`; the
//! scratch record beside it holds the cost probes and the RED arm (a head-first build disagrees
//! with first-match on a duplicate id). Registration: after `add_eval_ir_e5`, in both the EvalIr
//! bundle and `STAGES` (needs `ir_nat_eqb_ne_trans`, `ir_nat_eqb_sound` from
//! `add_eval_ir_lzd_fresh`).

